Third-party components
----------------------

firmware/
    The Intel HEX firmware files (PknLdr.hex, extracted from the OEM
    F235Ldr.sys, and Pakon7.hex) are third-party device-bootstrapping
    artifacts from the OEM Pakon software, with their own separate terms.
    They are NOT covered by the AGPL and are not a work of this project. See firmware/README.md for provenance and the legal
    note.

Rust crates (rust/Cargo.toml, versions pinned in rust/Cargo.lock)
    Compiled into the app's binary, each under its own license (mostly MIT
    and/or Apache-2.0): among them nusb, axum, tokio, tao, wry, muda,
    ndarray, rayon, image and jpeg-encoder. Not distributed as part of this
    source tree; cargo downloads them.

Unicorn (unicorn-engine, unicorn-engine-sys)
    The CPU emulator that runs the OEM DLLs, built from source by its crate
    and linked into the binary. GPL-2.0 (with bundled QEMU and GLib parts
    under their own terms). Not distributed as part of this source tree.

WebView2Loader.dll (Windows installer only)
    Microsoft's WebView2 loader, shipped beside Pakon.exe from the
    webview2-com-sys crate under the Microsoft WebView2 SDK license. Not
    distributed as part of this source tree.

oem/, profiles/
    Files from the original Kodak/Pakon F-X35 software, used as-is: the
    colour engine PakonIMAu.dll, its scene-balance parameters, the DX
    product-code table (oem/ansel/common/common-ProdCodeTable.dpi), the
    Digital ICE dust removal library DMLDICELib.dll (Applied Science
    Fiction), and the colour profiles and correction data (© Eastman Kodak
    Company). They are
    NOT covered by the AGPL. See oem/README.md and profiles/README.md.

test/fixtures/eeprom/
    Eight unmodified EEPROM section dumps (base F-135 serial 2233, F-135+
    serial 16402) from Ali Bosworth's pakon-reference, credited contributor
    Mats Fagerberg. CC BY 4.0, not covered by the AGPL. Used only as offline
    parser test fixtures. See test/fixtures/eeprom/README.md and LICENSE there
    for attribution and provenance.

